    "Markus Villig is the founder and CEO of Estonian ride-hailing firm Bolt Technology.",
    "Bolt offers ride-hailing, scooter and e-bike rentals, car-sharing and food delivery services in more than 850 cities in 50 countries.",
    "Villig founded Bolt in 2013 at age 19 after finishing high school with a 5,000 euro loan from his family. He then dropped out of college after one semester to work on the app full time.",
    "Bolt was valued at $8.4 billion in a January 2022 funding round led by Sequoia and Fidelity Management.",
    "In March 2025, Villig was appointed a board member at publicly traded Swedish buy-now, pay-later firm Klarna."
